  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1143 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026\n\nThursday still looks mild and dry. Cloud cover will decrease, with \nhigh temperatures in the 50s-60s over most of the CWA. We'll still \nsee some gusty south winds over the plains and the San Luis Valley, \nbut gusts will generally stay below 35 mph or so.\n\nOur next system will move in, starting Thursday Night and lasting \ninto Saturday. Snow amounts have continued to trend down with the \nlast few rounds of model solutions, though today's guidance shows \nthe main axis of the incoming trough moving through Colorado through \nthe day on Saturday. Once again, the heaviest snow will fall over \nthe San Juans, with long-range guidance remaining consistent around \nthe 3-6 inches mark for accumulations. Gusty winds will also make a \nreturn to most of the area, though the peak winds will largely \ndepend on the strength of the system as it moves through. Some of \nthese winds may be on the stronger side, though considerations for \nany highlights will need to wait until forecast confidence \nincreases, since there is still some variation in the strength of \nthe system between models. \n\nAs the system moves through, the area will cool off considerably, \nwith cool and mild conditions lasting into early next week.",
